{ The pawn push looks tempting. Can your king prepare a better route first? } 1. Kd7 { Your king takes a detour. It can enter e7 without losing the g6 pawn. [%cal Ge6d7] } (1. Kd6 { This route through d6 keeps the result exactly the same. } 1... Ke8 { Also winning. Your king still finds a way around the pawn wall. [%cal Bf8e8] }) (1. Kd5 { Another good square, d5. The result stays with you. } 1... Ke7 { This wins too. Your king reaches the far side of the wall by another path. [%cal Bf8e7] }) (1. Ke5 { Your king can take the e5 path instead. Nothing changes. } 1... Ke7 { Still winning: your king goes around the wall from here as well. [%cal Bf8e7] }) (1. f6 { The pawn advances before your king has reached the useful squares. } 1... Kg8 2. f7+ 2... Kf8 3. Ke5 3... Ke7 { The result has changed: his king slips into e7 first and blocks the way your king needed around the wall. [%cal Rf8e7] }) 1... Kg8 { His king steps back. Where can yours take the next important square? } 2. Ke7 { Your king reaches e7. Now the f pawn can help open a route to promotion. [%cal Gd7e7] } (2. Ke8 { The e8 square is equally good for your king. The result stands. } 2... Kh8 { Also winning. Your king slips around the pawns just as well this way. [%cal Bg8h8] }) (2. Kd6 { Going to d6 costs you nothing. The result is unchanged. } 2... Kf8 { This route wins too, and your king still gets around the wall. [%cal Bg8f8] }) (2. Kd8 { Your king has another good try in d8. Same result either way. } 2... Kh8 { Also winning. Your king finds another door around the pawn wall. [%cal Bg8h8] }) (2. Ke6 { Your king can go to e6 instead. It still keeps the result. } 2... Kf8 { Still good: your king still circles the wall in time. [%cal Bg8f8] }) (2. Kc6 { The square c6 works just as well for your king. The result does not change. } 2... Kh8 { This also wins. Your king reaches the far side of the wall regardless. [%cal Bg8h8] }) (2. Kc7 { Heading to c7 is fine too. Same result, different road. } 2... Kf8 { Also winning. Another path around the wall works for your king. [%cal Bg8f8] }) (2. Kc8 { Your king could step to c8 instead, and the result holds. } 2... Kh8 { This wins as well. Your king still turns the corner past the pawns. [%cal Bg8h8] }) 1-0


