{ Your g pawn has two starting speeds. Choose the one that gets the timing right. } 8... g5 { Two squares! You need to reach g3 while his king is on h1. [%cal Gg7g5] } (8... Kg4 { The g4 square is tempting, but the result changes there. } 9. Kg2 9... h3+ 10. Kf2 10... Kh4 11. Ke1 { The result has changed: the pawn arrives on g3 at the wrong moment this way. [%cal Rf2e1] }) (8... g6 { One square gives the wrong timing. Watch where his king can wait. } 9. Kg1 9... g5 10. Kh1 10... Kg4 11. Kg2 11... Kf5 12. Kf3 { The pawn timing is wrong. His king can wait without allowing the breakthrough. [%cal Rg2f3] }) 9. Kg1 { His king has only this move. Keep the pawn coming. } 9... g4 { One more step sets up the final push. [%cal Gg5g4] } (9... Kg4 { Your king's route through g4 changes the result. } 10. Kg2 10... Kf5 11. Kf3 11... g4+ 12. Ke2 { This move gets the timing wrong, and the result has changed. [%cal Rf3e2] }) 10. Kh1 { His king is in the corner. This is the moment to break through. } 10... g3 { Your pawn forces a capture or makes its own way to g2. [%cal Gg4g3] } 11. hxg3 { His pawn takes. Which pawn keeps your promotion route alive? } 11... hxg3 { Your new g pawn has the king beside it. Promotion follows. [%cal Gh4g3] } (11... Kxg3 { This time g3 is the wrong square. The result changes. } 12. Kg1 12... Kh3 13. Kf2 13... Kh2 14. Kf3 { The result changes here, because his king can now meet the pawn safely. [%cal Rf2f3] }) (11... Kg4 { Moving the king abandons your last pawn. That gives away the win. } 12. gxh4 12... Kxh4 { Your pawn is gone. Bare kings draw; recapture with the pawn instead. [%cal Rg4h4] }) 0-1


