{ A pawn breakthrough creates a passed pawn. Push to b6 and sacrifice to make one run. [%cal Yb5b6] } 1. b6 { The middle pawn breaks the chain. One neighboring pawn will get through. [%cal Gb5b6] } (1. Kg2 { Your king has another good try in g2. Same result either way. } 1... Kg6 { Also winning. The sacrifice plan is still there. This king move only delays it. [%cal Bh7g6] }) (1. Kh2 { Your king can also try h2, but that changes the result. } 1... b6 2. cxb6 2... cxb6 3. axb6 3... axb6 { The result changes here: your pawn sacrifices no longer clear the a column in time. [%cal Ra7b6] }) (1. Kg1 { The g1 square looks natural for your king, but it changes the result. } 1... b6 2. axb6 2... axb6 { Your pawns remain blocked. Waiting gave Black time to stop the breakthrough. [%cal Ra7b6] }) (1. c6 { A wing pawn goes first. The middle pawn cannot open a path in time. } 1... bxc6 2. Kg2 2... cxb5 3. Kf3 3... a6 { This costs you the breakthrough. Your sacrifices stop clearing the a column. [%cal Ra7a6] }) (1. a6 { This pawn goes first, but it cannot remove both neighboring guards. } 1... bxa6 2. b6 2... axb6 3. c6 3... b5 { The result flips: the a column never opens for your pawn this way. [%cal Rb6b5] }) 1... axb6 { He takes with the a pawn. Push your c pawn to c6 and remove the last guard. [%cal Yc5c6] } 2. c6 { Your second sacrifice pulls the b pawn away from the a column. [%cal Gc5c6] } (2. cxb6 { Advancing to b6 instead changes the result. } 2... cxb6 3. axb6 3... Kg8 4. Kg2 4... Kf7 { The result has changed, because your sacrifices no longer clear the a column. [%cal Rg8f7] }) (2. axb6 { This pawn push to b6 throws the result away. } 2... c6 3. Kg1 3... Kg6 4. Kg2 4... Kf6 { Your plan to clear the a column collapses here, and the result changes. [%cal Rg6f6] }) (2. a6 { The square a6 seems natural, but the result changes here. } 2... bxa6 3. c6 3... b5 4. Kg1 4... b4 { The a column stays shut this way, and the result has changed. [%cal Rb5b4] }) (2. Kg2 { Stepping to g2 changes the result instead of keeping it. } 2... bxa5 { Either wing pawn can be taken. He chooses the a pawn and keeps his c pawn. } 3. Kf3 3... a4 4. Ke4 4... Kg6 { This move lets Black seal the a column. The result has changed. [%cal Rh7g6] }) 2... bxc6 { He takes again. Push your a pawn to a6 and let it run. [%cal Ya5a6] } 3. a6 { The a column is clear. Your pawn reaches promotion before his pawns can. [%cal Ga5a6] } (3. Kg1 { Your king heading to g1 throws the result away. } 3... bxa5 4. Kh1 4... a4 5. Kh2 5... Kg7 { The result has changed: your sacrifices needed a different order to clear the a column. [%cal Rh7g7] }) (3. Kh2 { The square h2 seems fine, but the result changes here. } 3... bxa5 4. Kh3 4... Kh6 5. Kg4 5... Kg6 { Clearing the a column needed exact timing. This move throws it away, and the result changes. [%cal Rh6g6] }) (3. Kg2 { This king move to g2 is a step too far. The result changes. } 3... bxa5 4. Kf2 4... a4 5. Ke3 5... a3 { The result has changed: Black gets to close the a column before your pawn arrives. [%cal Ra4a3] }) (3. axb6 { Running the pawn to b6 costs you the result. } 3... cxb6 4. Kg2 4... Kg6 5. Kf1 5... Kf6 { Here the sacrifice sequence breaks down, and your a column never clears. [%cal Rg6f6] }) 1-0


