{ That pawn can be captured. First make sure your king will not lose the race. } 2. Kg2 { Your king steps closer before taking. The timing, not the free pawn, comes first. [%cal Gh1g2] } (2. f4 { This pawn's route through f4 changes the result. } 2... exf4 3. Kh2 3... g3+ 4. Kh3 4... Kd2 { The result has changed: your king needed one more step closer before the race began. [%cal Rd1d2] }) (2. fxg4 { A free pawn is tempting. Your king has not gained the move it needs. } 2... e4 3. Kg2 3... e3 4. Kf3 4... Kd2 { The e pawn wins the race. Move your king closer before capturing. [%cal Rd1d2] }) (2. Kg1 { Your king can also try g1, but that changes the result. } 2... gxf3 3. Kf2 3... e4 4. Ke3 4... Ke1 { This starts the pawn race too early, and the result has changed. [%cal Rd1e1] }) (2. Kh2 { The h2 square looks natural for your king, but it changes the result. } 2... gxf3 3. Kg3 3... Ke2 4. Kg4 4... e4 { The result changes here. Your king is a tempo short in the race that follows. [%cal Re5e4] }) 2... Kd2 { His king steps away. Can you now take without falling behind? } 3. fxg4 { Now both sides can run their pawns. The race is level, and the position is a draw. [%cal Gf3g4] } (3. Kf2 { Stepping to f2 changes the result instead of keeping it. } 3... gxf3 4. Kxf3 4... Kd3 5. Kf2 5... e4 { Racing now instead of improving your king first changes the result. [%cal Re5e4] }) (3. Kg3 { Your king heading to g3 throws the result away. } 3... gxf3 4. Kxf3 4... Kd3 5. Kf2 5... e4 { The result has changed: his e pawn wins the race this way. [%cal Re5e4] }) (3. f4 { The pawn to f4 looks fine, but it changes the result. } 3... exf4 4. Kf2 4... Kc1 5. Ke2 5... Kc2 { This skips the improving move your king needed, and the result changes. [%cal Rc1c2] }) (3. Kg1 { The square g1 seems fine, but the result changes here. } 3... gxf3 4. Kf2 4... e4 5. Kg3 5... Ke2 { The result has changed. The race starts one move too soon. [%cal Rd2e2] }) 1-0


